<title>SPAIN: Spain &quot;very good chance&quot; to be EMU founder -Rato.</title>
<headline>Spain &quot;very good chance&quot; to be EMU founder -Rato.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato reiterated on Tuesday that Spain will be among the founding members of the European single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;...Even in a very uncertain period as the one we are going through at present, we have a very good chance to be in the first European Monetary Union wave, a thing we would not have believed just a few months ago,&quot; Rato said in a radio interview.</p>
<p>He also said Spain was taking a new attitude toward stability with its commitment to lowering inflation and the public deficit.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
